      "BARBARA: Please don't turn this into a contest of wills--\nCOOK'S ASSISTANT: It's bad karma to welsh on a bet, Constance.",
      "SUSAN: Oh, a pointer here and there, not really worth a mention-- May I have a tiny bit more wine, please?\nBARBARA: You'll never guess who else has some news. I'm officially a business. Banquets by Barbara. Tomorrow I have a meeting about catering a party-…",
      "BARBARA: If you were having more than thirty guests I'd suggest a buffet, but a sit down lunch is more elegant.\nASSISTANT: Perdonme, Senora. La Senora Rose ha recibido una llamada urgente.",
      "SUSAN: My, this is really--I haven't had a Christmas like this since-- ever.\nBARBARA: It\"s a short. I said something was wrong with the lights last year--I don\"t think we should--",
      "SUSAN: Nothing for you either, missus?\nBARBARA: I'm going."
    ]
